  Two things worth knowing:

  - This is an idle-vs-absolute-agnostic single knob. If sessions are meant to expire 2h after [3mlast activity[0m rather than
    2h after [3mlogin[0m, that distinction lives in whatever consumes this value, not here — and [38;5;153mserver.js[39m is currently just
    a stand-in that prints it.
  - Nothing else in the repo reads [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES[39m, so there's no caller to update and no persisted sessions to
    migrate. Existing sessions, if any real implementation had them, would keep their old expiry until reissued.

